 Aggregate across 10 driver source trees, confirmed by reading actual SOURCE
 FILE licence headers (not the bundled COPYING file alone -- two of them,
 apogee's and sbig's, are stale "Library GPL v2" text left over from before
 upstream's own 2.1 relicense, contradicted by every .cpp header in both
 directories). See core/rpm/indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers.spec's own
 License: comment for the full per-vendor reasoning.

Files: indi-apogee/* indi-asi/* indi-fli/* indi-playerone/* indi-mi/*
 indi-sbig/* indi-toupbase/* indi-fishcamp/*
Copyright: The respective vendor driver authors and the INDI Library
 contributors
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
 Confirmed per vendor by reading actual .cpp header grants (spot-checked
 one representative source file per directory, not a full per-file audit):
 every one of these eight directories explicitly grants "version 2.1 ... or
 (at your option) any later version", contradicting apogee's and sbig's own
 stale bundled COPYING.LIB text (plain "Library GPL v2", no "or later"
 clause) where present. indi-fishcamp/indi_fishcamp.cpp added 2026-08-27,
 same grant verbatim.
 .
 On Debian systems the full text of this license can be found in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1.

Files: indi-inovaplx/*
Copyright: i.Nova Technologies
License: LGPL-2.0-only
 The ONLY signal in this directory is its bundled COPYING.LIB (the same
 stale "Library GPL v2" text as apogee's and sbig's) -- unlike the eight
 directories above, no source file here carries a licence header of its
 own, so there is no "or later" grant to upgrade the tag with. The
 conservative, defensible reading is the plain v2 text as written.

Files: indi-aagcloudwatcher-ng/*
Copyright: Lunatico Astronomia and the INDI Library contributors
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
 All seven source files grant "either version 3 of the License, or (at your
 option) any later version" under the plain GPL, and the directory ships the
 matching GPL-3 text as LICENSE.txt -- one of the few drivers here where the
 bundled file and the source headers agree.
 .
 On Debian systems the full text of this license can be found in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3.

Files: indi-nightscape/*
Copyright: The Celestron Nightscape driver authors and the INDI Library
 contributors
License: LGPL-2.0-only
 No source file in this directory carries a licence header at all. Its
 bundled COPYING.LIB -- the GNU Library General Public License version 2 --
 is the only statement of terms, so it governs, and it is shipped as the
 package's licence text. This is the one driver here whose bundled text is
 an exact match for its grant.
 .
 On Debian systems the full text of this license can be found in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.

Files: indi-openogma/*
Copyright: The OpenOGMA driver authors and the INDI Library contributors
License: AGPL-3.0-only
 Neither source file carries a licence header, so the bundled LICENSE.txt --
 the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 -- is the only statement of
 terms and governs. The Affero clause obliges operators who offer a modified
 version over a network to provide source to its users; it places no
 additional condition on redistributing this package.
 .
 The full text is shipped with the binary package. Debian's
 /usr/share/common-licenses does not carry the AGPL.

Files: indi-orion-ssg3/* indi-atik-efw/*
Copyright: The Orion StarShoot and Atik EFW driver authors
 and the INDI Library contributors
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
 Read per file: indi-orion-ssg3/orion_ssg3.cpp and indi_orion_ssg3.cpp, and
 all three files in indi-atik-efw, grant "version 2.1 ... or (at your
 option) any later version". indi-orion-ssg3/orion_ssg3.h carries no
 header and states no contradicting grant.
 .
 indi-orion-ssg3 bundles a LICENSE which is the GPL-3 text, contradicting
 every source header in its own directory. It is NOT shipped: a GPL text
 beside LGPL code overstates the terms in the direction that can mislead a
 redistributor. The same call indi-ocs's contradictory file gets.
 .
 indi-atik-efw has NO relationship to indi-atik or the Atik vendor SDK,
 which this project excludes on licence grounds -- checked directly rather
 than inferred from the shared name prefix: its CMakeLists.txt calls
 find_package for INDI and Threads only.
 .
 On Debian systems the full text of this license can be found in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1.

Files: indi-nexdome/* indi-talon6/* indi-ocs/* indi-starbook-ten/*
Copyright: 2019 Jasem Mutlaq
 2017 Rozeware Development Ltd
 2014/2023 Jasem Mutlaq, Ed Lee
 The Vixen Starbook TEN driver authors and the INDI Library contributors
License: LGPL-2.0-only
 Read per file across all four directories (2026-09-09), every file
 accounted for: each grants "the GNU Library General Public License version
 2 as published by the Free Software Foundation" with NO "or later" clause.
 That makes them LGPL-2.0-only, the same conservative reading indi-inovaplx
 already gets here and for the same reason -- there is no later-version
 grant to widen the tag with.
 .
 Four files in indi-starbook-ten (indi_starbook_ten.cpp/.h,
 starbook_ten.cpp/.h) carry no licence header at all. They state no
 contradicting grant, so the rest of the directory governs.
 .
 THE TEXT SHIPPED WITH THESE PACKAGES IS LGPL-2.1, NOT LGPL-2.0. That is a
 deliberate decision (Will, 2026-09-09): indi-3rdparty contains no LGPL-2.0
 text anywhere, checked rather than assumed -- indi-starbook-ten/COPYING.LESSER
 is 2.1 and libinovasdk/LICENSE.lib is a vendor notice. The alternatives were
 shipping no licence text or shipping a file from outside the source tarball.
 The License field above, which is what tooling and downstream consumers
 read, states the actual grant; only the accompanying text is the nearest
 available rather than the exact one.
 .
 indi-ocs additionally bundles a LICENSE.txt which is the GPL-2 text,
 contradicting every source header in its directory. That is a real
 contradiction rather than the staleness indi-apogee and indi-sbig carry, so
 it is not shipped -- a GPL text beside LGPL code would overstate the terms.
 .
 On Debian systems the full text of the LGPL-2.1 can be found in
 /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1.

